---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
	title="Kilnbook for school and college ceramics departments"
	description="Wheel bookings between classes, firing queues for one or two kilns, and semester courses with rosters. Kilnbook for school and college ceramics departments."
>
	<section class="band-dark page-hero">
		<div class="wrap">
			<p class="eyebrow">For schools &amp; colleges</p>
			<h1>Wheels, kilns and classes, on the school timetable.</h1>
			<p class="lede narrow">
				One or two kilns, a semester of courses, and students who want a wheel in the gap between
				classes. Kilnbook keeps wheel bookings, firing queues and class rosters in one place, so the
				ceramics room is not run from a clipboard on the door.
			</p>
			<a href="/contact" class="btn">Book a demo</a>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section section-alt">
		<div class="wrap">
			<p class="eyebrow">How it fits</p>
			<h2>Three things a ceramics department juggles</h2>
			<div class="cards">
				<div class="card">
					<h3>Wheels between classes</h3>
					<p>
						Students reserve wheels, hand-building tables and the slab roller in one-hour blocks. You
						decide how many hours a week they get and how far ahead they can book, and freed-up slots
						appear on the calendar right away.
					</p>
					<a href="/features/wheel-time">Wheel and table booking</a>
				</div>
				<div class="card">
					<h3>One queue per kiln</h3>
					<p>
						Each kiln has its own queue for bisque and glaze firings, with a firing log of the date,
						cone, schedule and who loaded it. Students get a text when their pieces come out.
					</p>
					<a href="/features/firings">How firing queues work</a>
				</div>
				<div class="card">
					<h3>Courses for the semester</h3>
					<p>
						Set each course up once as a fixed series. Instructors get their own login with the
						roster, mark attendance from the studio tablet and leave notes for the next instructor.
					</p>
					<a href="/features/classes">Classes and packs</a>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="wrap section narrow">
		<h2>Which plan fits a school?</h2>
		<p>
			Most departments run one or two kilns. The Starter plan covers one kiln, and the Studio plan
			covers up to 3 kilns, with unlimited members and wheel and table reservations. If you add a
			fourth kiln, you can move to Collective at any point in the month.
			<a href="/pricing">Compare plans</a>.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="wrap section narrow">
		<h2>Questions schools ask</h2>
		<div class="faq">
			<details>
				<summary>Do you offer pricing for schools?</summary>
				<p>
					Yes. School ceramics programs and registered nonprofits get 30% off any plan. Mention it
					when you book a demo.
				</p>
			</details>
			<details>
				<summary>We have two kilns. Which plan do we need?</summary>
				<p>
					The Studio plan. It covers up to 3 kilns, so you have room for one more. The Starter plan
					covers a single kiln.
				</p>
			</details>
			<details>
				<summary>Can I import our students from a spreadsheet?</summary>
				<p>
					Yes. Upload a CSV with names and emails, and we map the columns for you during setup.
				</p>
			</details>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="cta-band">
		<div class="wrap">
			<h2>Get the ceramics room off the clipboard.</h2>
			<p>See how Kilnbook works with your kilns, wheels and semester timetable.</p>
			<a href="/contact" class="btn btn-dark">Book a demo</a>
		</div>
	</section>
</Base>
